I like the idea of Frakir, but this falls afoul of one major tenet I
have right now: "No new artifact weapons".

Right now the vast majority of artifacts _are_ weapons, and while
weapons are important, they're not the be-all, end-all of the game;
adding another one simply adds overloading to a slot that's sufficiently
overloaded as it is.

Vlad's was an elegant way to give Vlad and two-handed weapons in general
some teeth, and Dirge supports an entire class variant; but even these 
weren't _strictly_ necessary.  Beyond that, though, I definitely want to 
avoid adding more artifact weaponry.  More hats, gloves, and shields are
next in line, since there's no competition for those slots right now.

